<LegalLayout title="Delete your Zenzu account">

<p>You can delete your Zenzu account, and everything stored with it, from
inside the app. No email or request to us is needed.</p>

<h2>How to delete your account</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Open the <strong>Zenzu</strong> app and sign in.</li>
  <li>Go to the <strong>Profile</strong> tab in the bottom navigation bar.</li>
  <li>Scroll to the bottom and tap <strong>Delete account</strong>.</li>
  <li>Type <strong>DELETE</strong> in the confirmation box and confirm.
  Deletion runs immediately and cannot be undone.</li>
</ol>

<p>If you can no longer sign in, write to
<a href="mailto:hello@zenzu.app">hello@zenzu.app</a> from the email address
on the account and we will delete it for you.</p>

<h2>What is deleted</h2>
<p>Deleting your account permanently removes all of it, right away:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Your account and sign-in identity, including your email address</li>
  <li>Your profile: display name, username, avatar and bio</li>
  <li>All decks, cards, images you added, and your review history</li>
  <li>Study statistics, streaks, achievements and placement test results</li>
  <li>Course progress and generated lessons</li>
  <li>Conversations with Lisa, the AI coach, and everything she remembered about you</li>
  <li>Workspace notes and writing attempts</li>
  <li>Saved videos, podcasts and listening positions</li>
  <li>Notification tokens for your devices</li>
</ul>

<h2>What is kept</h2>
<p>Two things outlive the account, and neither identifies you:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Shared content caches</strong> — for example subtitles fetched
  for a YouTube video. These are stored per video, not per person, and are
  shared by everyone who opens the same video.</li>
  <li><strong>Aggregated, anonymous statistics</strong> — counts that carry no
  account, device or personal identifier.</li>
</ul>

<p>There is no retention period and no grace period: once deletion completes,
your data is gone from our systems and cannot be restored.</p>

</LegalLayout>
